orage chip because 128  gigabyte modules are harder to get now  and they're more expensive than 256 is  but that is the point a pro machine  shouldn't come with 256 gigabytes in  2022 anyway dell starts the xps 13 plus  with 512 gigs now and that is a much  faster ssd than even the higher end  options of the macbook pro a lot of  these slowdowns wouldn't have happened  if it shipped with 512 as the base and  it would cost apple no more than two  dollars and seven cents to make it a  gig machine  yes that is how little one of those  chips costs likely even less since apple  orders in huge volumes so it's not  really the availability or the price of  the storage like apple apologists stated  but the fact that them spending two  dollars would lose them a 200 upgrade  that way more people are now doing  because of our testing so it is in fact  working in their favor so let's meet in  the middle apple how about raise this  profit margin machine to 1400 instead of  13 so all of the pro marketing machines  have 512 as a base you still get the  recycled design from 2016 with the 720p  webcam worst speakers than even the m1  air no fast charging no mag safe so you  have to use one of the two ports to  charge well then apple would probably be  in a similar situation where pros that  are on the budget would spend less and  not be guided up that perfect staircase  where moving up in spec and model it  just kind of makes sense because you  spend a little bit more and you do get  an increase in performance the m1  machines broke that because they were  too dang good but now the lineup works  perfectly the m2 air is for regular  people that don't have too high  expectations because of the fanless  design the m2 pro is for pros as it is  marketed but the base model is worse  than the m1 if you multitask so you need  the 512 but if you really want them to  chip to work as advertised you need the  16 gig model which isn't sold in stores  so if you need a quick you'll just spend  more money and go for a 14 inch for 2  000 bucks and if you do end up spending  1700 on a 16 gig 512 model well then  apple gets to make massive amounts of  profit and at that point they don't  really care that you didn't buy a 14  inch now a few more positives on this  machine the battery life is excellent it  just lasts forever like we've seen in  the last two weeks of use even if you're  pushing it with heavy cpu and gpu  workloads  it just keeps running and running and  then for light uses it is absolutely  insane now of course you don't get the  fast charging so when it does come time  to charge it will take you about twice  as long as the m2 macbook air now along  with that of course it has that fan and  that's what apple is marketing so for  those extended workloads it will perform  better and maintain the performance for  most of the tasks that you do  compared to them to macbook air which  will slow down for those extended uses  so that is a benefit now of course we  talked about the heating issues it  definitely gets hot a part of that is  because apple waits a long time to ramp  up the fans which you can fix yourself  but that is also a plus compared to  windows laptops where oftentimes even  downloading or you know extracting a  file web browsing you'll get fan noise  this thing acts like like a fanless  macbook most of the time which is a  benefit but overall this is probably the  worst macbook that apple has ever  released when you factor in the target  audience and the marketing as well as  the previous model that was released and  the other models that are currently  available and we believe that almost  nobody should buy it and unfortunately  that's probably what apple wants either  to spend more money get high specs a lot  of profit margins or for you to step up  and spend more money now sure many  people that will go in and that will buy  base model they will be happy with it  will be better than their old macbook  that is years old or a windows laptop  but that still doesn't make it ethical  or right uh making these kind of cuts  and making the product a lot worse than  it should be especially compared to  older cheaper machines that they  released that people absolutely loved  but you guys let us know your thoughts  down in the comment section below if  you're considering how it compares to a  14 inch or maybe even an m1 macbook air  that you can buy for 850 bucks check out  those videos right there click above to  subscribe this been max for max tech and  i'll see you in the next video  [Music]

